# .kamal/secrets.example — TEMPLATE for the Kamal deploy path.
#
#   1. cp .kamal/secrets.example .kamal/secrets
#   2. Fill in every value below (replace each <...>).
#   3. chmod 600 .kamal/secrets
# NEVER commit .kamal/secrets — only this .example file is tracked (see .gitignore).
# Every name referenced by env.secret in config/deploy.yml MUST be defined here,
# or Kamal errors at deploy time (the intended fail-fast safety net).
#
# Dotenv format note: single-quote any value containing backslashes (the PEM) so
# the parser keeps it LITERAL. Do NOT double-quote the PEM — double quotes expand
# \n into real newlines and the single-line key breaks. Kamal also supports
# $ENVVAR interpolation and $(command) substitution if you prefer those.

# --- Registry (the DEPLOYING USER's GH PAT with read:packages; NOT prisma-team's) ---
KAMAL_REGISTRY_PASSWORD=<github-personal-access-token-read-packages>

# --- GitHub App ---
GITHUB_APP_ID=<numeric-app-id>
GITHUB_APP_SLUG=<app-slug>
# PEM private key, SINGLE-LINE with literal \n escapes, single-quoted.
# Convert a .pem file:  awk 'NF {printf "%s\\n", $0}' app.private-key.pem
GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY='-----BEGIN RSA PRIVATE KEY-----\n<...>\n-----END RSA PRIVATE KEY-----\n'
# HMAC webhook secret:  openssl rand -hex 32
GITHUB_APP_WEBHOOK_SECRET=<hex-32-webhook-secret>

# --- Provider key: EXACTLY ONE active (uncommented). ---
# MUST match the single active provider name in config/deploy.yml env.secret.
# Precedence ANTHROPIC -> COPILOT -> OPENAI. Never leave an empty provider value;
# swap by commenting one and uncommenting another in BOTH files.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=<sk-ant-...>
# COPILOT_API_KEY=<github-pat-with-models-read>
# OPENAI_API_KEY=<sk-...>
